@startuml systems-overview
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title Conway's Game of Life - Systems Overview

package "Board System" as BoardSys #LightYellow {
  component "Board Management" as Board
  component "Sparse Grid Storage" as Grid
  component "Neighbor Counting" as Neighbors
}

package "Game Engine System" as EngineSys #LightCoral {
  component "Game Loop" as Loop
  component "Rule Engine" as Rules
}

package "Pattern System" as PatternSys #LightGreen {
  component "Pattern Library" as Library
  component "Pattern Placement" as Placement
}

package "Rendering System" as RenderSys #LightBlue {
  component "Cell Renderer" as Renderer
  component "DOM Pool" as Pool
}

' System interactions
EngineSys --> BoardSys : reads state\ncalculates next gen
PatternSys --> BoardSys : places patterns
RenderSys --> BoardSys : renders cells
BoardSys ..> EngineSys : provides board instance

note right of BoardSys
  **Responsibilities:**
  - Manage cell state (alive/dead)
  - Count neighbors efficiently
  - Validate coordinates
  - Provide sparse grid storage
end note

note right of EngineSys
  **Responsibilities:**
  - Run game loop (RAF)
  - Apply cellular automaton rules
  - Manage engine state
  - Control tick rate
end note

note left of PatternSys
  **Responsibilities:**
  - Define common patterns
  - Calculate pattern cells
  - Place on board
end note

note left of RenderSys
  **Responsibilities:**
  - Render cells to DOM
  - Pool DOM elements
  - Update cell positions
  - Optimize rendering
end note

@enduml
